{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04MS", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2b8361cf1394ae5343e42416b85472eb6c0671735f87c93819affe8617361bce", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe dimension of a scheme is just the dimension of its underlying\ntopological space.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:114d5bc8dc17c82d5aafea9d1bc729413efa388ef961a524b0fd7371429dce41", "unit_id": "tag:04MS:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04MS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\dim_x(X)$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\dim_x(X)$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-Krull}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-definition-Krull}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-dimension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1c08961d1d02d282e66d0b0adc8ee7acd52eda182c0d0406de18f569d69ff3d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:03400ada93dcf2e8a99e978520b611a0207bfaa8dafcad94aa57320c901f9063", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>dimension<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> is just the dimension of <MATH_0003>\nas a topological spaces, see\nTopology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For <MATH_0004> we denote <MATH_0005> the dimension of the underlying\ntopological space of <MATH_0006> at <MATH_0007> as in\nTopology, Definition <REF_0002>.\nWe say <MATH_0008> is the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>dimension of <MATH_0009> at <MATH_0010><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f955f0d35937f17761d5a4795e39dd0fe486e1fc8056cc2ad1a988a7e6c74e87", "unit_id": "tag:04MT:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04MS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$n$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nT_0 \\subset T_1 \\subset \\ldots \\subset T_n\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$n$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xi_n \\leadsto \\xi_{n - 1} \\leadsto \\ldots \\leadsto \\xi_0\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-scheme-sober}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:058a3e9d2892c75289a310a763beb24d74ced2115dfe43e0707eba02d5a41d58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62e7eb26d065890de5e1f052c7a0b0e0a9ce3ab2e421f72e81155228a2a31855", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAs a scheme has a sober underlying topological space\n(Schemes, Lemma <REF_0001>)\nwe may compute the dimension of <MATH_0001> as the supremum of the lengths <MATH_0002>\nof chains\n<MATH_0003>\nof irreducible closed subsets of <MATH_0004>, or as the supremum of the lengths <MATH_0005>\nof chains of specializations\n<MATH_0006>\nof points of <MATH_0007>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe4341180686a997fc751e5c1f289b77d57d8c682341867c6d967beb534b8c2a", "unit_id": "tag:04MS:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04MS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\dim_x(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-dimension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3972fe0890809c7d8847952177cc7cea5bcbe46d92dabce37fecf860e54b55fd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:67fdcbe3868dd8e96a3294635dbf5f164b45bff01d5bac23138ae6568053d073", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equal\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The dimension of <MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The supremum of the dimensions of the local rings of <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0004> The supremum of <MATH_0004> for <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:255ae16f118f90d8b4cf65f4882dea7fd180457798c97e3d73c11c70566449cd", "unit_id": "tag:04MU:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04MS", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xi_n \\leadsto \\xi_{n - 1} \\leadsto \\ldots \\leadsto \\xi_0\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\xi_i$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\xi_0$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\dim_x(X) \\geq \\dim(\\mathcal{O}_{X, x})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\dim_x(X)$", "MATH_0009": "$x$", "MATH_0010": "$\\sup_{x \\in X} \\dim_x(X) \\geq \\dim(X)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\sup_{x \\in X} \\dim_x(X) \\leq \\dim(X)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\dim(U) \\leq \\dim(X)$", "MATH_0013": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-specialize-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:50ae9c7b26ded77e60ff4c048ee78c8931f16421005217a9c9aa0e898a85c535", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5c3fe7695cb8d6eea6b0019bb79f09c4babf82a09be33c6c4eba5090c7921196", "source_text": "Note that given a chain of specializations\n<MATH_0001>\nof points of <MATH_0002> all of the points <MATH_0003> correspond to prime ideals\nof the local ring of <MATH_0004> at <MATH_0005> by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence we see that the dimension of <MATH_0006> is the supremum of the dimensions\nof its local rings. In particular <MATH_0007>\nas <MATH_0008> is the minimum of the dimensions of open neighbourhoods of\n<MATH_0009>. Thus <MATH_0010>. On the other hand,\nit is clear that <MATH_0011>\nas <MATH_0012> for any open subset of <MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70d00d77375620cea156034b310b42c89e6dbcf1b44a51bfe29021b3b7a75aa4", "unit_id": "tag:04MU:proof"}
